1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,578
An AI, quote, solved,

2
00:00:01,699 --> 00:00:03,575
unquote, a $1M maths

3
00:00:03,575 --> 00:00:04,991
problem. That is the

4
00:00:04,991 --> 00:00:06,461
headline. Here is the

5
00:00:06,461 --> 00:00:08,426
contested version. OpenAI says

6
00:00:08,426 --> 00:00:09,732
its agents proved that

7
00:00:09,732 --> 00:00:11,312
a forced Navier-Stokes fluid

8
00:00:11,312 --> 00:00:12,003
can blow up.

9
00:00:12,278 --> 00:00:14,264
On 8 September, it announced

10
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:16,075
that around 10,000 agents,

11
00:00:16,196 --> 00:00:18,292
running for about 88 hours,

12
00:00:18,412 --> 00:00:19,949
produced that proof, with

13
00:00:19,949 --> 00:00:21,595
a further 17 hours to

14
00:00:21,595 --> 00:00:22,791
formalise it in Lean.

15
00:00:23,065 --> 00:00:24,810
Forced versus unforced matters

16
00:00:24,810 --> 00:00:26,237
here, and OpenAI itself

17
00:00:26,237 --> 00:00:27,214
says it will not

18
00:00:27,214 --> 00:00:28,125
claim the prize.

19
00:00:28,399 --> 00:00:30,561
3 days later, 25 Fields

20
00:00:30,561 --> 00:00:32,416
Medallists published a statement

21
00:00:32,416 --> 00:00:34,051
titled A Severe Misalignment

22
00:00:34,051 --> 00:00:35,247
of AI in Mathematics.

23
00:00:35,521 --> 00:00:36,443
The work is not

24
00:00:36,443 --> 00:00:38,144
peer-reviewed, and a priority

25
00:00:38,144 --> 00:00:39,615
dispute has been reported.

26
00:00:39,889 --> 00:00:41,316
Big claim, big pushback.
